As the ocean's waves crashed onto the shore,
A symphony of sound, a dance of the tide;
The sand, a canvas, waiting to be told,
A story of the sea, in patterns bold.

The waves swept up, a swirling vortex of blue;
The sand, a swirling mass, as the ocean pulled through;
The patterns formed, a intricate design,
A poem of the sea, in a language divine.

The waves receded, the sand, a tranquil scene;
The poem, a reflection, of the ocean's sheen;
The meaning, a mystery, yet to be told;
A message from the sea, in a language old.

The poem read: "The tides of life, ebb and flow;
The waves of change, crash on the shore below;
The sand, a symbol, of the moments we hold;
The ocean's wisdom, a story to be told."

The poem ended, the waves, a gentle hush;
The sand, a peaceful calm, a soothing rush;
The meaning, a question, that still remains;
What secrets does the ocean, in its poem, contain?!

